# The Lantern in the Roadhouse (side quest, docs/story/side_quests.md): the Grey Goose roadhouse on the Old Svalich Road
# burned twenty winters ago, and every night since a lantern has hung in its upstairs window, though there's no upstairs
# any more (data/locations/svalich_roadhouse.json). The innkeeper's ghost, Wenzel, keeps it lit. **Twist:** the light isn't a
# welcome, it's a warning: the winter the snow shut the road, his wife and sons ate the guests, and he nailed them in
# the cellar and burned the house over them, and they didn't die. **Escalation:** they've been scratching at the
# trapdoor every night this month, and tonight the nails give. Reached from Arik's one-word rumours from level 2
# (village_of_barovia/arik:rumors) and the roadhouse by night. Every line here is unvoiced for now.

# --- Arik's rumour (village_of_barovia/arik:rumors jumps here) ---

~ arik
quest the_roadhouse_lantern rumored
Arik: Grey Goose. Lantern. No upstairs.
-> village_of_barovia/arik:menu

# --- The lantern (prop roadhouse_lantern) ---

~ lantern
if quest.the_roadhouse_lantern == done
Narrator: An old lantern lies in the weeds of the taproom, cold, its glass cracked. Nothing holds it up any more.
-> END
endif
if night
Narrator: A lantern hangs in the empty air where an upstairs window used to be, burning steadily, with nothing holding it up and no wall around it.
-> END
endif
Narrator: In daylight there's nothing in the air where the upstairs window was. On the hearth below, a lantern with its glass blacked by twenty years of smoke, cold to the touch, and full of oil.
-> END

# --- The innkeeper, by night (npc roadhouse_innkeeper) ---

~ innkeeper
if not quest.the_roadhouse_lantern or quest.the_roadhouse_lantern == rumored
quest the_roadhouse_lantern asked
endif
if flag.roadhouse_innkeeper_met
Wenzel: Still here. Go on. The crossroads is an hour. There's no room.
-> innkeeper_menu
endif
set roadhouse_innkeeper_met
Narrator: Under the lantern, in what's left of the taproom, a man in an apron stands behind a counter that's mostly charcoal. You can see the hearth through him.
Wenzel: Travellers. Wenzel, I kept the Goose. Turn round. Go on to the crossroads. There's no room at the Goose. There hasn't been for twenty winters.
-> innkeeper_menu

~ innkeeper_menu
* Who's the lantern for? -> for_whom
* [Insight DC 12] (Watch where he keeps looking.) -> looking | not_looking
* (Leave him to his lantern.) -> END

~ for_whom
Wenzel: For you. For anybody on the road. So you see the light, and see the walls, and see there's nothing here worth stopping for, and go on.
Wenzel: People stop for an empty house in the dark. They don't stop for a lit one. A lit one has somebody in it already.
-> innkeeper_menu

~ looking
Narrator: Every few words his eyes drop to the floor behind the counter, to a trapdoor nailed shut with more nails than it needs. Under it, faintly, something is scratching.
Wenzel: (Quietly.) They're hungrier this month. The nails are old.
-> innkeeper_menu

~ not_looking
Narrator: A dead man, keeping a light. That's all you can tell.
-> innkeeper_menu

# --- The ledger (prop roadhouse_ledger) ---

~ ledger
set roadhouse_ledger_read
Narrator: A guest book, swollen with damp, the last pages still legible. The snow shut the road early that year. No guests for nine days. The oats gone. The salt pork gone.
Narrator: Then, in Wenzel the innkeeper's careful hand: "Two guests. A tinker and his boy, from the Gates." And in another hand, round and childish, underneath: "Mama made a stew."
Narrator: After that, a few more names, a few days apart. Then nothing.
-> END

# --- The trapdoor (prop roadhouse_trapdoor) ---

~ trapdoor
if flag.roadhouse_cellar_beaten
Narrator: The trapdoor hangs open on one hinge. The cellar below is quiet, and smells only of old smoke.
-> END
endif
if not quest.the_roadhouse_lantern
Narrator: A trapdoor nailed shut, with more nails than any trapdoor needs.
-> END
endif
Narrator: A trapdoor behind the counter, nailed shut with three times the nails it needs. Something under it is scratching. When you crouch, it stops, and listens.
if flag.roadhouse_ledger_read
interject tag:blunt: Mama made a stew.
endif
* (Pull the nails.) -> open
* (Leave it shut.) -> END

~ open
if night
Wenzel: (From behind you, very quietly.) Don't. Please. That's my wife. Those are my boys. I burned the house over them and they didn't die.
endif
Narrator: The nails come out easily. Too easily: half of them were already loose, pushed up from below. The trapdoor lifts by itself before you've touched it.
combat roadhouse_cellar

# --- After the cellar, by night (npc roadhouse_innkeeper) ---

~ after
quest the_roadhouse_lantern done
Narrator: The innkeeper stands by the trapdoor with his hands in his apron, looking down into the dark for a long time.
Wenzel: The winter the snow shut the road, she fed the boys. That's all she did. Fed the boys. I found out on the tenth day, and I nailed the door, and I lit the thatch, and I sat down by the hearth to wait.
Wenzel: I kept the light so no one else would stop. Twenty winters. It's very tiring, being a warning.
Wenzel: Under the hearthstone. Everything we had. And my youngest's pipes; he played them to keep the rats out of the oats. Take them. I'd like to put the lantern down now.
Narrator: He sets the lantern on the hearth. It goes out. So does he.
give pipes_of_the_sewers
gold +50
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 kip_smudgewick +1: You let the innkeeper of the Grey Goose put his lantern down
-> END
